# Bootstrap first (enforced once per conversation)

This is a Cognition Stack consumer project. Bootstrap runs **once at the start of each new chat** — not on every follow-up message or topic change within the same chat.

## First turn only — MCP discovery

On the **first agent turn** of a new conversation (before any Read/Grep/Shell):

1. Read `.cursor/cogstack-bootstrap.json` for required blocks.
2. Call `open_block` for **every** listed block in **one parallel batch**.
3. Then work normally for the rest of this chat.

A hook blocks other tools until required blocks are opened, then **stays open** for all later prompts in this conversation.

## Do not re-bootstrap on follow-ups

"Also add…", "now let's…", refinements, and new sub-topics in the **same chat** → execute directly. Do **not** re-run bootstrap or re-open the standard block bundle unless the user says "reload cogstack" or context was compacted and procedure was lost.

## Re-bootstrap (rare)

Re-open `cogstack-agent-procedure` only after context compaction or when the user explicitly asks.
